  "result": "Excellent! All 44 tests pass (including 12 new tests for `addLine` and `removeLine`). Here's what I've added:\n\n**New error codes in `src/errors.js`:**\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND`: No line with that SKU on the invoice\n- `NOT_DRAFT`: Invoice must be in draft status to modify it\n\n**New functions in `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`** \u2014 Adds or increases a line:\n   - If the SKU is new, adds it as a new line with data from the catalogue\n   - If the SKU already exists, increases that line's qty\n   - Returns `NOT_DRAFT` if invoice status isn't 'draft'\n   - Validates qty (positive integer) and SKU (must exist)\n   - Returns new invoice without mutating the original\n\n2. **`removeLine(invoice, sku)`** \u2014 Removes a line:\n   - Removes the line with the given SKU\n   - Returns `NOT_DRAFT` if invoice status isn't 'draft'\n   - Returns `LINE_NOT_FOUND` if SKU isn't on the invoice\n   - Returns `NO_LINES` if it would remove the last line\n   - Returns new invoice without mutating the original\n\n**Comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Adding new lines and updating existing SKUs\n- Validation errors (NOT_DRAFT, QTY_INVALID, UNKNOWN_SKU, LINE_NOT_FOUND, NO_LINES)\n- Immutability of original invoice objects\n- Invoice structure preservation (customerId, issueDate, status remain unchanged)",
